; GDI32.DEF
;
; The functions the Windows 98 SE / Me build may import from GDI32.dll:
; the import library is made from this list (llvm-dlltool -k), and
; tools/win9x_check.py fails a linked image that imports anything else.
;
; Each name here is exported and implemented by the GDI32 of Windows 98
; Second Edition and of Windows Me: Windows 95 functions (the pixel-format
; and SwapBuffers ones come with OpenGL 1.1 for 95, and are in 98's GDI32;
; Get/SetDeviceGammaRamp are 98's), ANSI versions only.

LIBRARY GDI32.dll
EXPORTS
BitBlt@36
ChoosePixelFormat@8
CreateCompatibleBitmap@12
CreateCompatibleDC@4
CreateDIBSection@24
CreateFontA@56
CreateFontIndirectA@4
CreatePen@12
CreateSolidBrush@4
DeleteDC@4
DeleteObject@4
DescribePixelFormat@16
ExtTextOutA@32
GdiFlush@0
GetDeviceCaps@8
GetDeviceGammaRamp@8
GetObjectA@12
GetPixelFormat@4
GetStockObject@4
GetTextExtentPoint32A@16
GetTextMetricsA@8
PatBlt@24
Rectangle@20
SelectObject@8
SetBkColor@8
SetBkMode@8
SetDeviceGammaRamp@8
SetDIBitsToDevice@48
SetPixelFormat@12
SetStretchBltMode@8
SetTextColor@8
StretchBlt@44
StretchDIBits@52
SwapBuffers@4
TextOutA@20
